Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 00:04:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add TABLE content block: dynamic columns/rows with color-safe
 headers

Creators can now add a Table block to any slide with a fully dynamic
grid editor: add/remove columns and rows freely (min 1 column, rows
can go to zero), edit every header and cell inline, and set an
optional caption.

Header styling: a curated set of brand-palette color swatches plus a
free custom color picker. Rather than hardcoding white header text
(which would go unreadable against a light custom color like gold or
mint), header text color is computed automatically at render time
from the chosen fill using a WCAG-style relative-luminance contrast
check against both white and ink, picking whichever wins. This
guarantees a readable header regardless of what color a creator
picks, now or with any future preset changes - the alternative
(trusting creators to only pick safe colors) is exactly the kind
of thing that quietly breaks a lesson's readability months later.

Implementation:
- app/admin/lessons/actions.ts: added TABLE to the lessonBlockTypes
  Zod enum (missing this causes addLessonBlock to reject the new
  block type outright) and to defaultBlockContent (2x2 starter grid,
  moss-blue header). blockContentFromForm reads a single hidden JSON
  field (table_data) rather than trying to reconstruct a 2D grid from
  repeated form-field names, sanitizes to a consistent rectangular
  shape matching the header count, and drops fully-blank rows.
- components/LessonBuilderWorkspace.tsx: TABLE registered in
  blockTypes and labelForBlockType; blockSummary now shows a
  column x row count or the caption in the block list. The editor
  keeps headers/rows in local state (same pattern as the existing
  Flashcard editor), rendered as a real inline-editable table with
  add/remove controls per row and column, synced to a hidden JSON
  input and a header_fill hidden input for submission.
- components/LessonBlockPreview.tsx: new TableBlock component -
  responsive (horizontal scroll on narrow screens), zebra-striped
  rows, optional caption bar, colored header row with the computed
  contrast-safe text color. Shared by both the builder preview and
  the live student-facing lesson player (BuilderLessonPlayer), since
  both already render through this one component.

Does not touch any of Codex's OBE files (app/admin/obe/actions.ts,
lib/obe.ts, types/obe.types.ts, LessonOutcomeManager.tsx,
AssessmentMetadataEditor.tsx, CourseQuizOutcomeMapper.tsx,
ObeActionForm.tsx, or the migration) - verified via diff, zero
changes.

Verified with a full npm run build - compiles and type-checks clean,
same two pre-existing unrelated warnings, zero new ones.
